      "content": "The setting is the Kumalo home in Ndotsheni after they have received letters. \n\n---\n### 📖 Concept & Thought Process (How to Understand It):\n* **The Concept / Rule:** In literature exams, \"setting\" always has two parts: **place** (where the characters are physically located) and **time/circumstance** (what is happening or the immediate context of the scene).\n* **The Thought Process (How to Unpack It):**\n  1. *Step 1 — Identify the Place:* Scan the text for geographical markers or house mentions (e.g., Ndotsheni, Kumalo's church/home).\n  2. *Step 2 — Identify the Circumstance/Time:* Look at the immediate action or event that triggers the scene (e.g., the arrival of the mail carrier, the delivery of letters).\n* **How DBE Markers Score It (The 2-Mark Formula):**\n  * **Mark 1:** Correct location (Kumalo home / Ndotsheni).\n  * **Mark 2:** Correct circumstance/time (after the delivery of letters).\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** Whenever a question asks for the \"setting\" of a prose extract, never just write a place name. Always combine the location with the immediate action or time context to secure both marks!"
